On Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:18:05 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> Emails posted to the list have conventionally had the mail: prefix, but
> I want to be very clear about those commits as being messages. Use msg:
> prefix instead going forward.

Will do. From here on I commit each message as "msg: <Subject>", the
same form just commit-mail on the mail bookmark already produces.
This reply and the patch below are the first two done that way.

The one place left that still taught the old prefix was the
process-email skill on trunk, which committed "mail: Post [PATCH]
<subject>" and "mail: Reply to <subject>". That is fixed in
"[PATCH] claude/skills/process-email: Prefix list commits with msg:"
[1]. doc/guides/patch-workflow.org already describes msg:, and
nothing else on trunk mentions the prefix.

